From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 15:09:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] multitenant: shared-configstore governance spike
 validates Phase 1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds cmd/spike-shared, a separate binary that measures governance
plugin cost when one configstore is shared across all tenants. This
is the realistic Phase 1 design — Postgres with tenant_id row scoping.

Shared-configstore numbers (5 tenants):
  per-tenant heap:     24 KiB  (vs 880 KiB with per-tenant SQLite)
  cold-start avg:     178 us  (vs 60 ms with per-tenant migration)
  cold-start tenant 0: 441 us  (one-time migration baked in)
  per-tenant goroutines: 6   (vs 7 with per-tenant store)

That's a ~36x heap reduction and ~340x cold-start reduction vs the
per-tenant DB model. 10k tenants x 24 KiB = ~240 MiB heap — easily
viable.

cmd/spike-shared lives separately because the heap measurement is
sensitive to prior-section tear-down residue. Attempting it as a
final section inside cmd/spike produced negative deltas because GC
hadn't fully reclaimed Section 7's leaked SQLite handles by the time
the pre-snapshot ran. Forking a fresh process is cheaper than fixing
the contamination.

Reverts the broken Section 8 + --only flag from cmd/spike. Updates
SPIKE_FINDINGS.md headline table with all four configurations side
by side. Phase 1 is greenlit.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
